  "Mentalist": [
    {
      "label": "Telepath",
      "_note": "greyman is the corpus model, and this lands where greyman lands. It reads DC 6 / oAP 60 — a mental blast costs 10 points a die, so 60 active points is 6 DC where a blaster's is 12. Phil's IF(DC*5 > oAP) picks the oAP term, which is the honest read: the attack is expensive, not weak.\n\nOMCV/DMCV 8/8 is +10 of X on its own — the archetype's whole identity, and greyman runs the same. It pays for it in OCV 4, DCV 6, DEX 15 and thin defences.\n\nBuilt with a 40-point Resistant Protection first and it scored +5.9%. A term-by-term diff against greyman put 70% of the gap in ONE place: dAP compounds against DCV x DEF x rDEF, so doubling the force field nearly quadrupled the term (2.0 -> 8.8). greyman's shape — DEF 18, rDEF 12, dAP 36 — is the right one. A mentalist is squishy on purpose.\n\nMental Defense is genre-essential AND deliberate: Phil's sheet folds it into EGO ('include Mental Defense in this total'), so 10 points of it takes EGO 20 -> 30 and is worth ~+4 of X. It is the only archetype where a defensive power scores on the offensive side of the ledger.",
